{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>The threshing-floor of Atad.</b> It was surrounded by thorn-bushes, and our Rabbis interpreted (Sotah 13): after the name of the event — that all the kings of Canaan and the princes of Ishmael came for war, and when they saw the crown of Joseph hanging on the bier of Jacob, they all stood and hung their crowls on it and surrounded it with crowns like a threshing-floor surrounded by a fence of thorns."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 50, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:04:24.184784564Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}